Technical Design: The Compliance-Aware RAG Engine
1. The Core Challenge: The "Swiss Cheese" Problem
In enterprise HCM, a document (like a compensation philosophy) might be 90% public to managers but 10% restricted based on specific legal entities. Standard RAG retrieves chunks without "knowing" the internal sensitivity of the paragraph.
2. The Multi-Layered Retrieval Architecture
To solve this, we move away from "Simple Search" to Attributed Retrieval.
•	Layer 1: Deterministic ACL Filtering (The "Hard" Filter) Instead of letting the LLM decide what is relevant, the Nexus Gateway intercepts the query. It retrieves the user’s OAuth2/IAM identity and generates a Dynamic Security Filter.
o	Implementation: We use Vector Metadata Filtering. Every chunk in the Vector Database (e.g., Vertex AI Search) is tagged with a permission_bitmask.
o	Operation: The query is rewritten to: (Search Query) AND (user_bitmask & chunk_bitmask != 0).
•	Layer 2: Entity-Level Redaction (The "Soft" Filter) If a document is retrieved that contains PII (Personally Identifiable Information) the user shouldn't see, the Privacy Agent (a lightweight, regex-and-NLP-based service) redacts the text before it is passed to the LLM's context window.
3. Verification & Determinism (The "Truth" Engine)
To eliminate hallucinations in payroll/compliance queries:
•	Chain-of-Verification (CoVe): The engine doesn't just provide an answer. It must cite the Source-of-Truth ID and the Policy Version Timestamp.
•	Reference Checking: A secondary "Verifier Agent" takes the generated output and cross-references it against a Structured Knowledge Graph of payroll rules to ensure the math adds up.
4. Handling Global Data Sovereignty (The "Silo" Problem)
For L6 impact, we must handle the "Logical vs. Physical" constraint we discussed earlier.
•	Regional Ingestion Pipelines: Data from EU users is embedded and stored in europe-west1, while US data stays in us-central1.
•	The Global Orchestrator: The Nexus-Intelligence layer acts as a Federated Query Engine, sending sub-tasks to regional agents to ensure data never crosses a sovereign boundary during the retrieval process.
